  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The question defines the Nino 3.4 index as an anomaly relative to a 1950-2014 monthly climatology, so this fragment fixes what the anomaly is measured against and how ENSO events/outliers are judged (on anomalies, with persistence), which controls both the standard deviations and the |anomaly| > 1.0 °C counts.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each source's Niño 3.4 index as the anomaly of its own regional mean against its own monthly climatology for 1950-2014, matched to each calendar month; `compute_enso_nino_index` with `climatology='woa23'` on model output would put the model's mean-state bias into the index.",
        "State the climatology and the baseline (1950-2014) with the result; the amplitude statistics here use calendar months (January–December), not DJF/MAM season means, so do not mix season conventions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The amplitude statistics (population std over 780 months and per calendar month) are computed from monthly-mean `tos`, and this fragment warns that any variance/amplitude derived from monthly means differs from the online, higher-frequency diagnostic and must be stated as such.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The monthly climatology is the plain mean of that calendar month's values over the years of the baseline (no day weights); day weights (`temporal_aggregate`) apply only to averaging over a period spanning different calendar months.",
        "Monthly variance within a month cannot be recovered from monthly means: the std over the 780 months is inter-month/interannual only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model-versus-ERSSTv5 amplitude bias and the ranking of the three models depend on which cells of each source actually enter the Nino 3.4 average, so a common mask/domain over the sources is needed before biases are compared.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "the comparison is a scalar amplitude per source from its own regional index, with no cell-by-cell field comparison or multi-model ranking on a shared ocean mask."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The four sources sit on different grids (CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native `gn`, GFDL-ESM4 is regridded `gr` at 1°, ERSSTv5 at 2°), which determines which operations on the Nino 3.4 box are exact and how masks and conservation behave.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its `tos` is already remapped to 180×360 (conserve_order1), so its index and mask are regridded ones; CESM2 (100 km) and MPI-ESM1-2-LR (250 km) differ in resolution by about 2.5, so amplitude differences partly reflect resolution — state this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "A Nino 3.4 SST average is a surface mean and must be area-weighted over the top level, not a simple cell average, so this fragment constrains the computation of each source's index.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 5S-5N, 170W-120W mean of `tos` must be area-weighted with the model's own `areacello` restricted to cells where `tos` is valid (NaN-aware weights): `compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'`; an unweighted mean over a curvilinear grid, or over latitude, is wrong.",
        "Area-weight the ERSSTv5 regional mean on its own 2° grid the same way before taking its index."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The question supplies each source on its own native grid with its own published cell areas, i.e. `areacello`, which this fragment defines as the tracer-cell horizontal area to be used for the area weighting.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each model's published `areacello` for the weights (`load_areas` records `area_source`); total ocean area differs between models by a per cent or so, so state the area each regional mean was taken over rather than rescaling one model to another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-experiments-historical-ssp245.md",
      "sha256": "be5515ae7b8c8826c4e329bddcd5cbadc8e3e000292b7f6e83e1537af36a990c",
      "reason": "The historical runs are coupled runs with free internal variability whose years are not synchronised with observed years, so comparing 1950-2014 model ENSO amplitude against ERSSTv5 over the same calendar window must be qualified.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The coupled historical runs have their own internal variability with one member each: a given year is not expected to match ERSSTv5, so compare statistics (total std, calendar-month std, exceedance counts), not individual years or event timing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "The model index is built from `tos`, the top-cell bulk temperature including under-ice water, not a skin temperature like the observed SST product, so this definition is a caveat on the model-versus-ERSSTv5 amplitude comparison.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk temperature of each model's top cell, including under-ice values near freezing (these are not missing); top cells differ (CESM2 0–10 m, GFDL-ESM4 0–2 m, MPI-ESM1-2-LR 0–12 m), so the compared amplitude is not the same layer depth in all models — state this caveat."
      ]
    }
  ],
